.TH KISA-CCE-SCAN 8 "2026-09-02" "KISA CCE Linux Scanner" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
kisa-cce-scan \- assess KISA CCE 2026 Unix-server criteria on supported
Linux systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kisa-cce-scan
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kisa-cce-scan
collects persistent configuration, manager-normalized configuration, and
runtime state for the 67 KISA CCE 2026 Unix-server criteria.
It supports Ubuntu Server 26.04 LTS and Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.x.
.PP
The scanner does not remediate configuration, reload services, refresh package
metadata, or contact external hosts.
A normal scan writes protected text and JSONL reports.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-root " PATH"
Inspect an existing offline filesystem directory rooted at the absolute
.IR PATH .
Runtime collection is disabled automatically.
The special path
.B /
remains a live-root scan.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
Write reports below the absolute
.IR PATH .
The directory must not be a symbolic link, must belong to the invoking user,
and must grant no permissions to group or other users.
A missing directory is created with mode 0700.
This option has no effect in sysctl explanation mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-checks " U-01,U-02"
Run only the comma-separated criterion codes.
Codes are case-insensitive, whitespace is removed, and duplicates are ignored.
Results retain catalog order rather than argument order.
.TP
.B \-\-no-runtime
Disable live service, listener, kernel-value, and native-validator collection.
A scan of the live root still requires root privileges.
.TP
.BI \-\-explain-sysctl " KEY"
Print the effective persistent and runtime interpretation of one sysctl key
instead of producing CCE reports.
This option cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-checks .
.TP
.B \-\-allow-unsupported
Continue after warning that the detected platform is unsupported.
This bypass does not make results authoritative for that platform.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the scanner version and exit.
.PP
Options that take values accept both
.B "\-\-option VALUE"
and
.B "\-\-option=VALUE"
forms.
Positional arguments are rejected.
.SH MODES
.SS Live scan
Scanning
.B /
requires effective UID 0, including when
.B \-\-no-runtime
is supplied.
Runtime collection uses trusted native utilities from fixed system paths when
available.
.SS Offline scan
An absolute
.B \-\-root
other than
.B /
maps logical system paths below that root and disables runtime collection.
Root privileges are not required, but the invoking user needs read and
directory-search permission for the image.
.PP
Offline results cannot establish active services, listeners, loaded kernel
values, or other live state.
Affected criteria may return
.BR MANUAL ,
.BR NOT_APPLICABLE ,
or
.BR ERROR .
.SS Sysctl explanation
The diagnostic output distinguishes the filesystem configuration model, active
loader model where available, runtime value, and detected drift.
It follows standard
.I sysctl.d
directory precedence, equal-basename replacement, lexical ordering, masks,
glob assignments, and exclusions.
It does not change kernel parameters or create CCE report files.
.SH REPORTS
When
.B \-\-output-dir
is omitted, a root invocation uses
.IR /var/log/kisa-cce-scanner .
A non-root offline invocation uses
.IR /tmp/kisa-cce-scanner-UID .
.PP
The scanner creates an owner-only temporary workspace and two randomized
mode-0600 files:
.TP
.I kisa-cce-HOST-TIMESTAMP.txt.RANDOM
Human-readable scanner metadata, criterion sections, evidence, and summary
counts.
.TP
.I kisa-cce-HOST-TIMESTAMP.jsonl.RANDOM
One JSON object per selected criterion followed by one summary object.
.PP
The hostname identifies the machine running the scanner, including during
offline analysis.
The command prints
.B text_report=
and
.B jsonl_report=
paths only after final integrity checks succeed.
An interrupted scan may leave incomplete report files whose paths were not
printed.
.PP
The JSONL file does not repeat the scanner, platform, root, runtime-mode, or
timestamp header from the text report.
Retain both files when those provenance fields are required.
.SH RESULT STATES
.TP
.B GOOD
Collected evidence conclusively satisfies the implemented criterion.
.TP
.B VULNERABLE
Collected evidence conclusively violates the implemented criterion.
.TP
.B MANUAL
Policy, intent, an approved exception, external state, or unavailable context
requires review.
.TP
.B NOT_APPLICABLE
Absence of the relevant service or feature was established.
.TP
.B ERROR
Required evidence could not be collected or parsed reliably.
.PP
A
.B GOOD
result is not a certification of the entire host.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No
.B VULNERABLE
or
.B ERROR
result was recorded.
.TP
.B 1
At least one
.B VULNERABLE
result and no
.B ERROR
result were recorded.
.TP
.B 2
Invocation, platform detection, collection, report writing, report integrity,
or at least one criterion produced an error.
.TP
.B 130
The process received SIGINT.
.TP
.B 143
The process received SIGTERM.
.PP
.B ERROR
takes precedence over
.BR VULNERABLE .
.B MANUAL
and
.B NOT_APPLICABLE
do not change the exit status by themselves.
.SH SECURITY
Run the scanner only from a trusted, root-owned installation or a protected
source checkout.
The public launcher clears the caller environment before loading private Bash
code.
Live native commands are restricted to fixed system paths and are subject to
ownership and write-permission checks.
.PP
Reports can contain sensitive host configuration.
Targeted redaction is defense in depth and does not replace review before
storage or transfer.
.PP
When
.B \-\-output-dir
points below an offline root, report files are written into that image.
.SH FILES
The following paths describe a package installed with
.BR prefix=/usr .
.TP
.I /usr/bin/kisa-cce-scan
Installed public command.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/kisa-cce-linux-scanner/
Default private Bash implementation directory.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kisa-cce-linux-scanner/criteria.tsv
Ordered criterion catalog.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kisa-cce-linux-scanner/VERSION
Scanner version.
.TP
.I /etc/os-release
Platform identification inside the live or offline root.
.TP
.I /var/log/kisa-cce-scanner/
Default live-root report directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a complete live scan:
.PP
.EX
sudo kisa-cce-scan
.EE
.PP
Run selected criteria:
.PP
.EX
sudo kisa-cce-scan --checks U-01,U-02,U-65
.EE
.PP
Inspect an offline filesystem:
.PP
.EX
kisa-cce-scan --root /srv/images/ubuntu-26.04 --no-runtime
.EE
.PP
Explain one sysctl key:
.PP
.EX
sudo kisa-cce-scan --explain-sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysctl (8),
.BR sysctl.d (5),
.BR systemd-sysctl.service (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR sshd_config (5),
.BR os-release (5)
.PP
KISA CCE 2026 Unix criteria:
.UR https://kreonet.github.io/kisa-cce-guide-web/unix/
.UE
